		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: OpenGD77 BluedV Android  Issue]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=430&amp;p=3528#p3528"><![CDATA[
Connect the gd77 to the phone with OTG cable, first press and hold the black side key when turning it on, this is important. change the channel to your access point, then, in TCPUART (transmission speed 115200), click on CONNECT, will the phone ask you with allow? click OK and then on the tcp server click SERVER, enter 2000 and START.<br>   press your start button (leaving TCPUART running in the background)<br>   start BLUEDV, configure, enable ser2net, enter ip 127.0.0.1 click send<br>   the radio should now say WAITING FOR TRACKING, click on the BLUEDV PHONE ICON and connect<br>   sometimes you may need to restart TCPUART<br>   If it doesn't work, verify that your phone is OTG compatible<br>   good luck<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=84">EA1MU</a> — Tue Jan 07, 2020 9:41 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
